[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1bqk1nr/ppppbppp/2n5/3Q4/2B1P3/2P2N2/P4PPP/RNB1K2R_b_KQkq_-_2_7"]

{ One more Scotch gambit trap: your queen has just jumped out to d5. }
7... d6 { He pushes his d pawn to let his bishop out, and it loses at once: his knight to h6 was the only defence. Can you punish it? } 8. Qxf7+ { Check! Your queen takes on f7, guarded by your bishop, and his king has only one square left. Now watch. [%cal Gc4f7][%tail] } (8. Ng5 { The knight jumps at f7 too, but it gives him a move. } 8... Ne5 { Level: his knight covers f7 and hits your bishop, and the mate is gone. [%cal Re5f7] }) (8. Nbd2 { The knight comes out, but that gives him time. } 8... Be6 { Slightly better for him: his bishop hits your queen and blocks the road to f7. [%cal Re6d5] }) (8. Bb3 { The bishop steps back, and the chance is gone. } 8... Be6 { Slightly better for him: his bishop hits your queen, and the mate is off. [%cal Re6d5] }) (8. O-O { Castling is safe, but he gets a free move. } 8... Be6 { Better for him: his bishop hits your queen and shuts off f7, and he keeps his extra pawn. [%cal Re6d5] }) (8. Be3 { The bishop comes out, but he gets time to defend. } 8... Be6 { Better for him: his bishop covers f7 and hits your queen, and he is still a pawn up. [%cal Re6f7,Re6d5] }) (8. Ba3 { The bishop aims at his d pawn, but f7 was the target. } 8... Be6 { Better for him: his bishop hits your queen, and he keeps his extra pawn. [%cal Re6d5] }) (8. Bf4 { The bishop comes out to f4, but it gives him time. } 8... Be6 { Better for him: his bishop blocks f7 off and chases your queen. [%cal Re6d5] }) (8. e5 { The pawn push hits his d pawn, but f7 was the target. } 8... Be6 { Much better for him: his bishop chases your queen away from f7, and he keeps his extra pawn. [%cal Re6d5] }) 8... Kd7 9. Be6# { Mate! Your bishop checks from e6, your queen guards it and covers e8, and his own pieces box in the rest. [%cal Gf7e8,Gf7e6] } 1-0


