{ The last Scotch gambit trap: your queen has just taken back on d4 and stands in the middle. }
6... d6 { His d pawn steps up to free his light bishop, a mistake: his knight to f6 had to come first. What did he leave unguarded? } 7. Qxg7 { Your queen grabs the pawn on g7 and hits his rook on h8. [%cal Gg7h8] } (7. Qd5 { The queen aims at f7, but he covers it. } 7... Be6 { Better for you, but his bishop covers f7, and the free pawn on g7 is gone. [%cal Re6f7] }) (7. O-O { Castling misses the pawn his move left hanging. } 7... Nf6 { About level: his knight on f6 blocks your queen's road to g7. [%csl Rf6] }) (7. Nc3 { The knight comes out, but it misses the pawn. } 7... Bf6 { About level: his bishop hits your queen and covers g7. [%cal Rf6d4,Rf6g7] }) (7. Bf4 { The bishop comes out, but the pawn on g7 was free. } 7... Be6 { About level: his bishop blocks your bishop's view of f7, and the chance is gone. [%cal Re6c4] }) (7. Nd2 { The knight comes out, and he gets time to guard his king side. } 7... Nf6 { Level: his knight comes out to f6, and the pawn on g7 is safe. [%csl Rf6] }) (7. Be3 { The bishop comes out, but he can hit your queen first. } 7... Bf6 { Slightly better for him: his bishop hits your queen, and the pawn on g7 is covered. [%cal Rf6d4] }) (7. Bxf7+ { The bishop takes on f7 with check, but the pawn on g7 was the prize. } 7... Kxf7 { Much better for him: his king took your bishop, and you got one pawn for it. [%csl Rf7] }) 7... Bf6 { His bishop hits your queen, and that is his last mistake: his light bishop had to go to e6 instead. Can you finish it? } 8. Qxf7# { Mate! Your queen takes on f7, guarded by your bishop, and his king has nowhere to go. [%cal Gc4f7] } (8. Qg3 { The queen runs from the bishop and misses a mate. } 8... Qe7 { Better for you: still a pawn up, but mate on f7 was right there. [%csl Rf7] }) (8. Bxf7+ { The check on f7 wins a pawn, but the queen could do more. } 8... Kd7 { Much better for you, but the queen on f7 would have given mate. [%csl Gf7] }) (8. Qxh8 { The queen grabs his rook, but his bishop takes her. } 8... Bxh8 { Lost for you: his bishop took your queen, and mate was right there. [%csl Rh8] }) (8. Qxf6 { The queen takes his bishop, but his queen takes back. } 8... Qxf6 { Lost for you: his queen took yours, and you got only a bishop. [%csl Rf6] }) 1-0
